WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:03.100
-The President is
still defending

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.501
his doctored math,
insisting that he was right

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:07.501
about Hurricane Dorian
hitting Alabama.

00:00:07.501 --> 00:00:09.968
For more on this, it's time
for "a closer look".

00:00:09.968 --> 00:00:13.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:17.100
Now, we know Donald Trump is
and has always been

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:19.767
a conspiracy theorist
and pathological liar

00:00:19.767 --> 00:00:22.567
who is completely detached
from reality.

00:00:22.567 --> 00:00:24.100
It's always been his brand.

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.167
It's just that back when he was
a New York real-estate buffoon,

00:00:27.167 --> 00:00:29.000
people didn't take it
that seriously.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.300
New Yorkers mostly ignored him

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:34.334
because that's what New Yorkers
do with crazy people.

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:38.767
New Yorkers reacted to Trump
the way you react to a guy

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.834
who gets on the subway
with a lizard on his shoulder.

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:43.300
That was Trump.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.834
Except in his case,
he has two lizards.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:54.501
In fact, Trump's
entire origin story is basically

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:57.968
that of a crazy guy who,
after years of being ignored,

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.968
finally heard,
"Hey, cool lizard."

00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.234
His entire campaign
for president started

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.734
as a desperate attempt to
get people to take him seriously

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.534
as he himself admitted
to his supporters

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:11.667
during a speech in 2016.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.467
-A lot of people have laughed
at me over the years.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.434
Now they're not laughing
so much, I'll tell you.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:18.801
-That is something a villain
would say in a superhero movie.

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.234
Don't believe me?

00:01:20.234 --> 00:01:22.467
Because that line is
almost verbatim

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:24.667
a line from the new Joker movie.

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.367
-A lot of people have laughed
at me over the years.

00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:28.267
Now they're not laughing
so much, I'll tell you.

00:01:28.267 --> 00:01:32.033
-Everyone laughed at me.
Well, no one's laughing now.

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:44.100
-Now, sometimes Trump lies
for the obvious reasons --

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.601
like, you know,
to cover up crimes.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:48.367
Sometimes he makes up weird
stuff for no apparent reason.

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:51.334
And then sometimes, there's
just little bits of junk

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:53.834
floating around in his polluted
brain that he belches up

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:56.934
during rambling speeches like
the time he claimed

00:01:56.934 --> 00:02:00.701
during a speech on trade that
Canadians were smuggling shoes

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:04.400
back across the border to avoid
paying tariffs on footwear,

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.434
tariffs that do not exist.

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:10.968
-There was a story two days ago
in a major newspaper

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.901
talking about people living
in Canada

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:16.400
coming into the United States
and smuggling things

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:21.400
back into Canada because
the tariffs are so massive.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:27.434
The tariffs to get common items
back into Canada are so high

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:29.701
that they have to
smuggle them in.

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:32.434
They buy shoes,
then they wear them.

00:02:32.434 --> 00:02:34.267
The scuff them up.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:37.000
They make them sound old
or look old.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:42.200
-They make the shoes sound old?
What does that mean?

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.667
Do they complain
about rap music?

00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.634
Do they hit the roof
of the apartment with a broom?

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:50.000
"Turn that racket down!

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:52.701
We got some boots
trying to sleep!"

00:02:52.701 --> 00:02:55.234
And, of course, it isn't just
that Trump lies,

00:02:55.234 --> 00:02:57.834
it's that he concocts
elaborate fantasies

00:02:57.834 --> 00:03:00.567
to justify those lies
even when they're contradicted

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:01.734
by playing video evidence

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.334
that you can see and hear
for yourself

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:06.767
like the time he accidentally
called the CEO of Apple,

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:10.467
Tim Cook, "Tim Apple"

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:13.601
and then tripled down
with a series of bizarre

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.067
and shifting excuses.

00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:16.567
-The President is
still playing clean-up

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:20.334
after the referred to Apple CEO
Tim Cook as "Tim Apple."

00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:22.334
-We appreciate it very much,
Tim Apple.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.667
-The coverage of Tim Apple

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:25.334
has apparently gotten
under Trump's skin.

00:03:25.334 --> 00:03:27.868
At Mar-a-Lago on Friday night
with no cameras present,

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:29.968
Trump reportedly explained
to a group of donors

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.300
what really happened.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.400
Axios reports Trump told
the donors that he actually said

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.534
"Tim Cook Apple," like,
really fast,

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:38.801
and the "Cook" part
of the sentence was soft

00:03:38.801 --> 00:03:41.234
but all you heard from the fake
news, he said, was "Tim Apple."

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:43.334
-A few days after that,
Trump wrote this.

00:03:43.334 --> 00:03:45.834
"At a recent roundtable meeting
of business executives

00:03:45.834 --> 00:03:49.367
and long after formally
introducing Tim Cook of Apple,

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:53.334
I quickly referred to Tim plus
Apple as 'Tim Apple'

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:56.334
as an easy way to save time
and words."

00:03:56.334 --> 00:03:59.767
-My favorite part of that tweet
is when he writes out

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:04.934
"Tim plus Apple," like
he's carving it into a tree.

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:07.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.567
Trump has been at war
with reality

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.334
virtually his entire adult life,
and that war took

00:04:14.334 --> 00:04:16.634
one of its most insane turns yet
this week

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:18.000
when the President
of the United States

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.801
spread disinformation
about a hurricane

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.501
and then repeatedly
went out of his way

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:23.000
to insist he was actually right.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.434
You might remember
this whole thing started

00:04:24.434 --> 00:04:25.701
when Trump tweeted
over the weekend

00:04:25.701 --> 00:04:27.667
that Alabama would be hit
by Hurricane Dorian,

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:30.601
and then 20 minutes later,
the national weather service

00:04:30.601 --> 00:04:33.667
had to tweet Alabama will not
see any impacts of Dorian.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:36.200
"We repeat --
No impacts from Hurricane Dorian

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.000
will be felt across Alabama."

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.400
That was 20 minutes later.

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.133
The National Weather Service

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:43.901
has to monitor
the President's tweets

00:04:43.901 --> 00:04:47.200
as closely as they monitor
actual hurricanes,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.734
which actually makes sense
because when you think of it,

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:54.100
Donald Trump is the hurricane,
except unlike regular Hurricanes

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:59.400
that eventually die down,
everyday, Trump blows harder.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.067
After he was corrected
by his own government,

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:02.801
Trump doubled down,
as you probably saw.

00:05:02.801 --> 00:05:06.367
Yesterday, he seemed to alter
a forecast on the storm's path

00:05:06.367 --> 00:05:09.133
from last week
with a circle added in Sharpie

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:11.100
to include Alabama.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:12.634
My favorite thing about this

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:15.400
is that he didn't even try
to blend it in.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.734
He could have at least sent
an intern to Kinko's

00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:19.501
to print up a new chart.

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:22.901
"So, yeah,
what are you trying to do here?"

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.000
"Uh, we want to fake
a hurricane map

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:30.334
to retrofit a lie the President
told to the American people."

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:34.200
"Okay.
When do you need it by?"

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.467
Trump is even too lazy
to lie convincingly,

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.667
and he used a Sharpie,
which gives it away

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.968
because the only person
in the world

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:43.434
who's famous for using Sharpies
is Donald Trump.

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:44.901
It is a dead give away.

00:05:44.901 --> 00:05:46.734
That's like turning to the
Avengers and saying,

00:05:46.734 --> 00:05:47.968
"All right, which one of you

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:50.067
shot me in the ass
with an arrow?

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:53.434
Hawkeye?
Was it you, Hawkeye?"

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:56.167
And then, later, Trump was asked
about the altered map,

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:58.267
and he was so flummoxed,
all he could do

00:05:58.267 --> 00:06:01.801
was barf up a lengthy,
incoherent word salad.

00:06:01.801 --> 00:06:05.067
-You showed us the map earlier
of the initial forecast.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:10.000
It appeared to have been
extended to include Alabama.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.934
Can you explain
how that came to be?

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:17.934
-No, I just know Alabama was
in the original forecast.

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:20.300
They thought it would get it
as a piece of it.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.400
It was supposed to go --
Actually, we have a better map

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.400
than that, which is
going to be presented

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:27.467
where we had many lines
going directly, many models,

00:06:27.467 --> 00:06:28.868
each line being a model,

00:06:28.868 --> 00:06:30.567
and they were going
directly through,

00:06:30.567 --> 00:06:32.868
and then, in all cases,
Alabama was hit.

00:06:32.868 --> 00:06:36.334
They actually gave that
a 95%-chance probability.

00:06:36.334 --> 00:06:38.267
It turned out that
that was not what happened.

00:06:38.267 --> 00:06:40.234
It made the right turn
up the coast.

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:41.501
Everyone's gonna be
in great shape

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:43.801
because we're gonna
take care of it, regardless.

00:06:43.801 --> 00:06:46.734
Regardless. But the original
path was through Florida.

00:06:46.734 --> 00:06:48.300
That was probably three days --

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.567
I think that's probably three,
four days old.

00:06:50.567 --> 00:06:53.868
-I thought you wanted to save
time and words!

00:06:53.868 --> 00:06:56.167
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.734
I'll make up for this.

00:06:58.734 --> 00:07:01.367
I'll make up for this.

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:04.868
I'll say Tim Apple, and that
will buy all that time back.

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:09.033
Bill Microsoft --
That's five minutes right there.

00:07:09.033 --> 00:07:11.467
Also, if it's three
or four days old,

00:07:11.467 --> 00:07:12.701
then why are you
telling us this?

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.467
Why are you showing us a map
of a hurricane

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:17.234
that's so out of date, you had
to edit it with a Sharpie?

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:20.868
At his next briefing, he's just
gonna hold up a map of Pangea.

00:07:20.868 --> 00:07:23.067
"So, this is
a little out of date.

00:07:23.067 --> 00:07:24.934
Little out of date,
but as you can see,

00:07:24.934 --> 00:07:26.868
all the countries are
crammed together, one land mass,

00:07:26.868 --> 00:07:29.234
and, uh, the hurricane,
it was gonna --

00:07:29.234 --> 00:07:33.167
it was supposed to hit all these
stegosauruses over here."

00:07:33.167 --> 00:07:36.934
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:07:36.934 --> 00:07:41.000
Then the reporter asked
a natural follow-up question --

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:44.400
Did you use a sharpie
to alter the map?

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:47.534
And Trump acted like he had
no idea what happened.

00:07:47.534 --> 00:07:49.334
-Is that map that
you showed today --

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:50.968
looks like it was almost, like,
a Sharpie.

00:07:50.968 --> 00:07:53.767
-I don't know. I don't know.
I don't know.

00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:58.734
-It is so damning how
he just keeps getting quieter.

00:07:58.734 --> 00:08:00.334
He's like a kid
who hit a baseball

00:08:00.334 --> 00:08:01.467
through his neighbor's window.

00:08:01.467 --> 00:08:02.167
"Who did this?"

00:08:02.167 --> 00:08:03.467
"I don't know.

00:08:03.467 --> 00:08:06.734
I-I don't know.

00:08:06.734 --> 00:08:08.133
[ Quietly ]
I don't know."

00:08:08.133 --> 00:08:11.067
Also, what do you mean
you don't know?

00:08:11.067 --> 00:08:13.667
Are you claiming someone else
defaced your map?

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:17.367
Like some prankster snuck in
and sprayed graffiti on here?

00:08:17.367 --> 00:08:19.300
"Yeah. They crept in here
and drew a circle

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.434
and Sharpie on it,
and then signed their names,

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:22.734
Tim plus Apple."

00:08:22.734 --> 00:08:25.367
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:08:25.367 --> 00:08:28.167
Then, last night,
Trump still couldn't let it go

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:30.834
and tweeted what he claimed was
a map of the original forecast

00:08:30.834 --> 00:08:33.267
dated August 28th, which didn't
prove anything anyway

00:08:33.267 --> 00:08:37.501
because it was four days before
his incorrect tweet on Sunday.

00:08:37.501 --> 00:08:39.334
-On Wednesday,
the President showed a map

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:41.701
trying again to prove
his incorrect point.

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:43.667
But weather experts say
the President was using

00:08:43.667 --> 00:08:45.133
an out-of-date map.

00:08:45.133 --> 00:08:47.167
There were
much fresher forecasts.

00:08:47.167 --> 00:08:48.767
-President Trump tweeted this.

00:08:48.767 --> 00:08:50.901
It's called a spaghetti model.

00:08:50.901 --> 00:08:52.400
It shows every possible path

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.334
the hurricane is forecasted
to take.

00:08:54.334 --> 00:08:57.100
-Those spaghetti models were
from August 28th.

00:08:57.100 --> 00:09:01.667
By the time the President
tweeted Alabama at 10:51 a.m.

00:09:01.667 --> 00:09:05.000
on Sunday, the forecast track
had moved well east.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:07.100
-These were all the computer
models, the spaghettis.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.567
-That's right. He tweeted a map

00:09:08.567 --> 00:09:10.400
of what's known
as the spaghetti models.

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:11.934
Of course,
Trump probably thought

00:09:11.934 --> 00:09:14.868
it was a map that tells you
where you can find spaghetti.

00:09:14.868 --> 00:09:16.367
"It's very helpful.

00:09:16.367 --> 00:09:20.868
I didn't even know you could get
spaghetti in Alabama, but..."

00:09:20.868 --> 00:09:22.501
So, the President
has already been corrected

00:09:22.501 --> 00:09:25.133
by his own government, altered
an official Hurricane forecast

00:09:25.133 --> 00:09:27.234
with a Sharpie, rambled on
about it at a press conference,

00:09:27.234 --> 00:09:28.634
and then tweeted about it,

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:31.767
and yet, somehow, this fever
dream has not come to an end

00:09:31.767 --> 00:09:33.801
because Trump woke up
this morning, and, again,

00:09:33.801 --> 00:09:36.367
railed off another deranged
tweet storm about it.

00:09:36.367 --> 00:09:38.334
Trump tweeted in the early days
of the hurricane,

00:09:38.334 --> 00:09:39.868
when it was predicted
that Dorian would go

00:09:39.868 --> 00:09:41.534
through Miami
or West Palm Beach,

00:09:41.534 --> 00:09:43.901
certain models strongly
suggested that Alabama

00:09:43.901 --> 00:09:45.267
and Georgia would be hit.

00:09:45.267 --> 00:09:47.267
And then Hurricane Dorian took
a different path

00:09:47.267 --> 00:09:49.067
up along the east coast.

00:09:49.067 --> 00:09:51.467
Why did you put that
in parenthesis?

00:09:51.467 --> 00:09:56.100
That's the only part
of the tweet that's correct.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:58.934
At this rate, Trump's gonna
start adding tiny footnotes

00:09:58.934 --> 00:10:02.067
to his tweets with the correct
information at the bottom.

00:10:02.067 --> 00:10:05.334
"I just nuked something...
a Hot Pocket in the microwave."

00:10:05.334 --> 00:10:09.834
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:10:09.834 --> 00:10:13.934
This whole thing perfectly
captures the constant exhausting

00:10:13.934 --> 00:10:15.834
bewilderment of living
through the Trump era.

00:10:15.834 --> 00:10:20.534
There's a very real humanitarian
crisis unfolding in the Bahamas

00:10:20.534 --> 00:10:23.601
and a dangerous Hurricane is
threatening the mainland U.S.,

00:10:23.601 --> 00:10:27.100
and, meanwhile, the President is
obsessing over a map he doctored

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:28.801
to defend
an embarrassing mistake

00:10:28.801 --> 00:10:30.501
that he is now repeatedly
lying about.

00:10:30.501 --> 00:10:33.033
Almost nothing that comes
out of his mouth is true.

00:10:33.033 --> 00:10:36.734
In fact, at any time he speaks,
the odds that he's lying are...

00:10:36.734 --> 00:10:39.667
-A 95%-chance probability.

00:10:39.667 --> 00:10:41.467
-This has been "A Closer Look."

